  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mo>&#8853;</mo></math> and <math><mo>&#8855;</mo></math> are two mathematical operators. If <math><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8853;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8855;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is equivalent to <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, then <math><mo>&#8853;</mo></math> and <math><mo>&#8855;</mo></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "keKiO",
      "text": "can be <math><mo>∨</mo></math> and <math><mo>∧</mo></math> respectively",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "S8gQg",
      "text": "can be <math><mo>∧</mo></math> and <math><mo>∨</mo></math> respectively",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HrChG",
      "text": "can both be <math><mo>⇒</mo></math> ",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "YprIJ",
      "text": "can be <math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> and <math><mo>⇔</mo></math> respectively",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
